**Definition 3.5 (exact unary layout inverse).** From either parser's
node list use Find for the fixed outer socket paths. Decode a tape at path
$p$ by repeating: if both children are absent stop at its trailing terminal;
otherwise require both children, parse the left $F_8$ cell, and continue at
$p1$. Each of its eight sockets must have exactly one terminal child, left
or right, giving that track bit. A finite-location socket may instead have
no child, giving absent. Scaffold parsing uses the fixed consecutive
floor/ceiling split. Reject malformed scaffolds, missing required child,
nonterminal bit child, extra socket children or missing fixed component.

Emit the raw 74 lists and finite vector. Re-run the component walker and
require equality with the complete parsed node list; this excludes unused
nodes. Check cursor/access-link consistency under the native carrier's
actual mark convention. Do not demand a valid source tree, sealed bank,
complete descriptor, valid active main code, or completed copy. Raw eight
tracks and absent locations are decoded literally. S/B→raw is asserted
on the actual carrier image, including its malformed-source/partial-code
states; history decoding has the smaller domain in §7.

